00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:34.913
- So a lot of good news
here, so first of all,

00:03:34.913 --> 00:03:36.650
tell us about the research study.

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:39.810
- Sure, so it was very important for us

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:43.810
to get an independent
academic study on our program,

00:03:43.810 --> 00:03:45.430
to test the effectiveness of it.

00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:49.100
And we did a study with
Professor David Arnold

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:51.300
from the University of
Massachusetts in Amherst,

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:54.230
and he just released his results publicly.

00:03:54.230 --> 00:03:57.400
And the study was a randomized
control trial study,

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:59.730
which is the gold standard
of academic studies.

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:04.730
Were there two groups of
randomly selected students,

00:04:04.953 --> 00:04:09.470
and one group gets the Khan
Academy Kids intervention

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:12.650
and one get is the control group.

00:04:12.650 --> 00:04:15.440
And so this was a study
of four and five year olds

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:18.020
prior to entering kindergarten.

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:20.490
And they were from low income families

00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:25.490
with an median annual
income of about $24,000.

00:04:26.650 --> 00:04:31.260
And so what we saw was
that in a 10 week study,

00:04:31.260 --> 00:04:33.640
the kids that were using Khan Academy Kids

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:38.270
saw substantial increases in
their pre literacy skills.

00:04:38.270 --> 00:04:40.546
So they were tested pre test,

00:04:40.546 --> 00:04:45.080
with the test of preschool
early literacy, TOPEL test.

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:48.350
And then post test and we saw the gains

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:49.650
were really substantial.

00:04:49.650 --> 00:04:51.980
They were at the beginning of the study

00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:54.750
about upper 34th percentile likely,

00:04:54.750 --> 00:04:56.160
due to the effects of poverty.

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:59.170
And then after the 10 weeks
of using Khan Academy Kids

00:04:59.170 --> 00:05:00.830
for 20 minutes a day.

00:05:00.830 --> 00:05:05.030
They were close to the national
average at 47th percentile.

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:07.683
And so the size of these
gains are substantial,

00:05:08.944 --> 00:05:11.100
they're equivalent to
what is typically found

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:13.550
in much more expensive intervention.

00:05:13.550 --> 00:05:16.510
So as an example, the phonological gains

00:05:16.510 --> 00:05:20.390
were comparable to those found
in an intervention of 25,

00:05:20.390 --> 00:05:23.323
one to one sessions with
a professional tutor.

00:05:25.919 --> 00:05:27.120
- I mean there's a lot
