00:05:46.070 --> 00:05:49.500
- Right because students,
particularly low income students,

00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:51.650
often enter the first day of kindergarten

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:53.300
and they're already behind

00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:55.690
in these critical pre literacy skills.

00:05:55.690 --> 00:05:58.860
Which are things like recognizing
letters of the alphabet,

00:05:58.860 --> 00:06:01.280
understanding letter sounds,
knowing their letter sounds,

00:06:01.280 --> 00:06:04.760
and understanding
phonological awareness skills,

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:07.130
being able to break down
sounds and words and sentences.

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:09.300
So these are really critical
to learning how to read.

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:12.150
So they start school behind
and then they don't catch up.

